meta {
  name: R9 Login OTP — cooldown vs resend-limit (B4)
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/send-otp/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-App-Platform: DeliveryApp
}

body:json {
  {
    "phone": "{{phone}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.body.error_code: isDefined
}

docs {
  B4 — two distinct throttle states that used to be conflated:
  - Fire this TWICE within 30s → the second is 429 with error_code OTP_COOLDOWN and NO
    second SMS is sent. Waiting the cooldown then retrying succeeds (§10.13).
  - Keep going until the hourly allowance is spent → 429 error_code OTP_RESEND_LIMIT,
    and Retry-After is the TRUE window reset (not the 30s cooldown that never clears it)
    (§10.14).
  - An unregistered number returns the SAME shape (no rider-enumeration oracle) (§10.15).
  Note: on the first (allowed) call the response is 200 with cooldown_seconds /
  resends_remaining and has no error_code — so this assert only holds on a throttled call.
}
